{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Time-Consuming)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Time-Consuming)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_~_using_the_answer_choices_(similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 ~ using the answer choices (similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(A_Variation_of_Solution_4)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (A Variation of Solution 4)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(using_factors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (using factors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheMathGeek_(Insane_SPEED-10_Seconds!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheMathGeek (Insane SPEED-10 Seconds!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A store increased the original price of a shirt by a certain percent and then lowered the new price by the same amount. Given that the resulting price was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fceca304ecdebbd0bcdbf2c1c7a312dd8a24465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the original price, by what percent was the price increased and decreased<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8960d40d67144344fa86ca431cc1d6491690c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$?$\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c1e0e981858634838534232fc85f65c0051489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }16\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }20\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }28\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }36\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the fraction of discount is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a53319606a05264d060c2637933a85c4ff5f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-x)(1+x)=0.84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />; so, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a532f2df8bc4961ade5bd30b9f17636f3e4a121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-x^{2}=0.84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fe77e47ee00090afd44d3200d11817f6b0ca55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^{2})=0.16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"19\" />, procuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f93bdedbfb19eab6b9d434eef736941084f26fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the price was increased and decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />%, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea98d2dcd8c69b8fb78a664d832d705e2574e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After the first increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> percent, the shirt price became <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe39e42d6606c6d94238ae851082c69f6d4219ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> times greater than the original. Upon the decrease in p percent on this price, the shirt price became <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8fabc4067cdd36172db1feab7dab083db3b806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> times less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe39e42d6606c6d94238ae851082c69f6d4219ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1456c54dddbb362340d2044fd82075f047be2f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-p)(1+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />. We know that this price is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> percent of the original, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84137dd0b788953a04bb612cfdd7cb80e86f86f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-p)(1+p) = 0.84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>From here, we can list the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff2bb2a43ff35bc9101f2c8412d99f1348595c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> and see which are equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee7b72bb8583d298352ecf342d773a27335a0fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01bac0c4eff5c2c7741c47d9fed9a4ea57cd92ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532f79402cd2d051c7bde5d1c1a6ecce07e3bc2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1cb003f50fac5a83e03dcf0fd02553e311c1269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 0.4 = 40 \\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" />, or choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea98d2dcd8c69b8fb78a664d832d705e2574e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n~TaeKim\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Time-Consuming.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Time-Consuming)\">Solution 2 (Time-Consuming)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Time-Consuming)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can try out every option and see which one works. By this method, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea98d2dcd8c69b8fb78a664d832d705e2574e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />. Note: We can make the simplifying assumption that we start with 100 dollars.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let x be the discount. We can also work in reverse such as (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee6ad27a51cbe0c2e1dbb259467c53b64461d0ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{100}{100-x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f8e72c4f632c228936596e4946f79ac9d71258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{100}{100+x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ecac8bbc3200842badf42fea8257b136dcbcd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24481e6599e2adf019ad761f0c39eccc8cacd5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100+x)(100-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d431fe7a13a7aa1a23a5059aaa6e50d29d0af367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 40, -40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be positive. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.7E_using_the_answer_choices_.28similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_~_using_the_answer_choices_(similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 4 ~ using the answer choices (similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 ~ using the answer choices (similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let our original cost be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b0fb10d0f7b619a323ff9dc4437be2611621826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 100.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> We are looking for a result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43c5c18a2e795ce6e83d885ac1d08fe50d797268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 84,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> then. We try 16% and see it gets us higher than 84. We try 20% and see it gets us lower than 16 but still higher than 84. We know that the higher the percent, the less the value. We try 36, as we are not progressing much, and we are close! We try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82907b270af72e1e0748c9521d35e493e2030575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{40\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"26\" />, and we have the answer; it worked.\n(OR: try (C) first to eliminate 2 answer choices)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28A_Variation_of_Solution_4.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(A_Variation_of_Solution_4)\">Solution 5 (A Variation of Solution 4)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (A Variation of Solution 4)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let our original cost be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751f8354c64df7687207c0df786c41cc883ab3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, so we are looking for a whole number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fff55d3e8fb02528b4d958cc78c75971743f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />. Also, we can see that (A), (C), and (D) give us answers with decimals while we know that (B) and (E) give us whole numbers. Therefore, we only need to try these two: (B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6a1da7f18069a90481296d18af7ca979fe3854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> increased by 20% = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4192f79c29f33aa59c4c4b86bd0696c09ccc6080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4192f79c29f33aa59c4c4b86bd0696c09ccc6080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> decreased by 20% = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffe927e858d3e82fbb56b9fe69a823086b7ab71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />, a whole number, and (E) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6a1da7f18069a90481296d18af7ca979fe3854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> increased by 40% = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6555c6c1a2c3ebc414f84b13a6455aff27fb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6555c6c1a2c3ebc414f84b13a6455aff27fb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> decreased by 40% = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa63ea576da6808fb01025d848144f9cb4ece95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, a whole number.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />% or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea98d2dcd8c69b8fb78a664d832d705e2574e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" /> is the answer.\n</p><p>~ SaxStreak\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28using_factors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(using_factors)\">Solution 6 (using factors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (using factors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First find the prime factors of 84. These are 2,2,3 and 7. Using this, try the answers. For example, 100*1.2/1.2. This is equal to 120*0.8. If you find the factors of 12 and 8, you find that there is no seven and too many 2's. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e60e69a849ed7e5c86536dd111d531ff0e40946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is out. Using the same method, you can find that 116*0.84 is out, as 84 already has all the factors of 84. 128*0.72 and 136*0.64 both don't have seven as a factor, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416720d7c4b5bedfcfa068fb54249fb906d19684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24a0169117609a4da88670f626d53cbf2250b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792d9e8d96fb6e51472071167bcdcc91e185b186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> is out.  This leaves 140*0.6, which has just the right amount of factors (2^2,3, and 7). Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea98d2dcd8c69b8fb78a664d832d705e2574e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~ParticlePhysics\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1OxwVtXXMzM\">https://youtu.be/1OxwVtXXMzM</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheMathGeek_.28Insane_SPEED-10_Seconds.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheMathGeek_(Insane_SPEED-10_Seconds!!)\">Video Solution by TheMathGeek (Insane SPEED-10 Seconds!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheMathGeek (Insane SPEED-10 Seconds!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKHSel-mi8Q\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKHSel-mi8Q</a>\n~TheMathGeek\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY\">https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY</a>\n</p><p>~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9HDVTfEtpQA\">https://youtu.be/9HDVTfEtpQA</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 8\">2019 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2